  "content": "Security tightened in Maitighar-Baneshwor area (Photos)\nShankar Giri\nThursday, October 9, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 9\nSecurity has been tightened in areas around Maitighar and New Baneshwor.\nA large number of Nepal Police and Armed Police Force personnel have been deployed in these areas. The Gen-Z group had filed a complaint with the police against former Prime Minister KP Sharma Oli and Home Minister Ramesh Lekhak.\nFollowing that, the ANNFSU, the student wing of the CPN-UML, also filed a complaint against Kathmandu Metropolitan City Mayor Balen Shah and Gen-Z Sudan Gurung.\nThe police have forwarded Gen-Z’s complaint to a high-level investigation commission, and they are also preparing to send the complaint filed against Balen Shah and Sudan Gurung to the same commission.\nTensions escalated after both sides began filing complaints against each other.\nAs a result, a high level of security alert has now been enforced in the Maitighar–Baneshwor area.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nBP Highway\nFlowers\nnational women team\nShankar Giri\nGiri is a photojournalist at Onlinekhabar.\nMore From the Author\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nMaitighar actor CP Lohani passed away\n1 year ago\nPolice arrest members of the Madhesi community for celebrating Dhoti Diwas in Maitighar\n2 years ago\nCCTV cameras being put up throughout Thamel to tighten security\n2 years ago\nHow local reinsurance brokers can push Nepal’s insurance industry forward\n3 years ago\nIED found at Maitighar Mandala, defused\n6 years ago\nMaitighar Mandala as restricted zone: Home Minister says Dr Govinda KC is authoritarian\n7 years ago\nMost Read\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\n12 stranded backpackers rescued from Langtang\nPM Karki chooses new social media accounts over Oli’s\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nPolitics\nWho do student unions stand for? Questions rise after Gen Z Movement\n1 day ago\nEconomy\nThai AirAsia to resume flights from Gautam Buddha International Airport\n1 day ago\nFestival\nFlowers ready for Tihar Festival (Photos)\n1 day ago\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n2 days ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n2 days ago",
